    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e63cc380_25d10440",
        "filename": "sdk/sdk.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 101,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-21T09:30:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t understand why it would complain about multiple  matching modules. When I added host_supported: true to the java libraries in sdk_test.go, it worked.\n\njava_library_host is not accepted as the containing APEX (which is HostAndDeviceSupported) will fail to find the device variant of the lib.\n\n    sdk_test.go:114: Android.bp:47:3: dependency \"myjavalib\" of \"myapex2\" missing variant:\n          arch:android_common\n        available variants:\n          arch:linux_glibc_common\n    sdk_test.go:114: Android.bp:39:3: dependency \"myjavalib\" of \"myapex\" missing variant:\n          arch:android_common\n        available variants:\n          arch:linux_glibc_common",
      "parentUuid": "c2911ac1_3917784b",
      "revId": "c5a47ca9a00a39bd7040a85e79214249aa57c6c2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8e419327_a2e3a807",
        "filename": "sdk/sdk.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 101,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-21T18:09:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "AddDependency has a fallback, if there is only one variant of a module it will take it regardless of the variations of the depending module.  The failure you showed is because you have an apex and an sdk module depending on myjavalib, but if you only had an sdk module depending on a host library it would probably accept it.  Can you use mctx.AddVariationDependencies(nil, ...), which will only accept dependencies with matching variations?",
      "parentUuid": "e63cc380_25d10440",
      "revId": "c5a47ca9a00a39bd7040a85e79214249aa57c6c2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
